# Xawery Project Rules

## Project Context
This is an e-commerce demo showcasing parametrized products with feature flags (LaunchDarkly).
Stack: Angular + Node.js + PostgreSQL + Prisma + LaunchDarkly.

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for all code
- Follow ESLint and Prettier configurations
- Use conventional commits (feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, test:)
- Keep commits small and focused

## Architecture Principles
- Feature flags: Server-side for security, client-side for UX only
- Auth: JWT with role-based access control (ADMIN, MANAGER, VIEWER)
- API: RESTful with Zod validation
- Database: Prisma ORM with PostgreSQL

## File Organization
- Shared types/DTOs in `packages/shared`
- Keep API routes thin, business logic in services
- Use dependency injection patterns
- Test files in `src/__tests__/` with `.test.ts` extension

## Testing
- Backend: Vitest for unit/integration tests
- Frontend: Vitest + Testing Library (when implemented)
- E2E: Playwright
- Use flag stubs for deterministic testing
- Test both flag ON and OFF scenarios
- Write tests for each new feature before committing
- Run `pnpm test` to verify all tests pass

## Commit Workflow
1. Make focused changes
2. Write/update tests for changes
3. Run `pnpm test` to ensure tests pass
4. Run `pnpm format` to format code
5. Use conventional commit messages
6. Update README if adding features

## Test Guidelines
- Test happy paths and error cases
- Mock external dependencies (database, APIs) when needed
- Keep tests focused and readable
- Use descriptive test names: "should do X when Y"

